														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1751457">
									

<p>Hrrrm. Okay&#8230; Well. I think a lot of this could have been written more simply, and would have improved the article. And much of the article's content feels like dead weight; it either doesn't add anything or isn't interesting/amusing enough.</p>
<p>But all that said, the use of UIU and all of the last interview log (which is funny and very nicely done) pushes me to an upvote. This article is actually a pretty good example of the value of ending on a high note.</p>
<p>EDIT: On second read, I should be clearer -</p>
<p>The first paragraph is really the worst in terms of 'dead weight'. It feels like anti-reader kryptonite. It may be in-universe useful, but it's not interesting to read and difficult to absorb.</p>
<p>Beyond that, the article could be improved by splitting up paragraphs for readability. Notably, splitting the 2nd Containment Procedures paragraph, and splitting the final Description paragraph (between &quot; Addendum 1862-10.&quot; and &quot;Of possible note&quot;).</p>
<p>I didn't feel I got enough out of the website logs, but they read as authentic &amp; others appear to like them, so take that critique with a grain of salt.</p>

							</div>

								
